\caption(The two regularizers summarize activities, rather than imposing a per-observation count of active coordinates. Pooled and split KL objectives are different quantities.)
\alttext(Complementary near-on/off rows and constant half-active rows both lead to identical unit means, L1 and KL penalties.)

> Executed four-leaf model and objective branches

Every variant has independent encoder/decoder weights and 2×784×64+64+784 = 101,200 learned
scalars in four tensors. There is no hard gate in this sigmoid code. The shape probe uses two
observations to show the actual batch-mean branch. Its output is the complete regularized
scalar objective; all reconstruction and penalty inputs remain in the traced graph. Graph style,
Blocks detail, shared linear scales, a two-pixel visibility floor, six sampled planes and eight
sampled neurons are explicit; exact shapes remain in labels and tooltips.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sparse_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore p(1601);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& x) {
        const auto net = n::models::SparseAutoencoder(p, x, .05f, .05f);
        n::model_stage("Sigmoid encoder: 784 → 64", x, net.code);
        n::model_stage("Independent sigmoid decoder", net.code, net.reconstruction);
        n::model_stage("Pixel MSE", std::vector<n::Tensor>{net.reconstruction, x}, net.mse);
        n::model_stage("Mean absolute activity", net.code, net.penalty.l1);
        n::model_stage("Batch mean per unit", net.code, net.penalty.unit_mean);
        n::model_stage("Clip mean to interior", net.penalty.unit_mean, net.penalty.clipped_mean);
        n::model_stage("Mean Bernoulli KL", net.penalty.clipped_mean, net.penalty.kl);
        n::model_stage(
            "Weighted L1 + KL",
            std::vector<n::Tensor>{net.penalty.l1, net.penalty.kl},
            net.penalty.total);
        return n::model_stage(
            "Complete regularized loss",
            std::vector<n::Tensor>{net.mse, net.penalty.total},
            net.loss);
      },
      "Sigmoid autoencoder with separate L1 and mean-unit KL branches");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Graph;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.max_neurons           = 8;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 6;
  const auto figure             = model.plot(n::zeros({2, 784}), options);
  if (p.count() != 101200 || p.size() != 4 || figure.parameter_count() != 101200)
    return 1;
  figure.save_svg("build/sparse_architecture.svg");
  std::print("| parameter | scalars |\n|---|---:|\n");
  for (const auto& name : p.names())
    std::print("| {} | {} |\n", name, p.at(name).numel());
}
```
