\caption(The complete differentiable objective, including both inputs to MSE and the two activity branches. Penalty coefficients introduce no learned leaves.)
\alttext(A branched tensor diagram connects sigmoid encoding to reconstruction MSE, absolute-activity mean and clipped unit-mean KL, then joins all terms into the scalar loss.)

> Genuine MNIST pools and provenance

Native preparation supplies the original balanced 1,000 fitting, 200 validation and 200 test
images. Fit/validation IDs are disjoint official training records; held-out IDs are official test
records. Pixels remain Float32 [0,1], flattened from [N,28,28,1] only at the dense model input.
The source manifest and IDs are retained. Labels affect gallery columns, never fitting or selection.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", cache.string());
  const auto      pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(cache / "saliency");
  n::NamedTensors data;
  std::print("| pool | images | per digit |\n|---|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int split = 0; split < 3; ++split) {
    const std::string name = split == 0 ? "fit" : split == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    data.emplace_back(name + "_images", pools[split].images);
    data.emplace_back(name + "_source_ids", pools[split].source);
    if (split == 2)
      data.emplace_back("test_labels", pools[split].labels);
    std::print(
        "| {} | {} | {} |\n", name, pools[split].images.size(0), pools[split].images.size(0) / 10);
  }
  n::save_npz("build/sparse_data.npz", data);
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "saliency" / "manifest.json",
      "build/sparse_data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
```
